        "original_id": "720a9df5-a1da-55dc-a39b-6b4f55cdc2ab",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Lucy Maud Montgomery, Anne Shirley\n- Products: Anne of Ingleside, Anne of Green Gables, Road to Avonlea\n- Places: Avonlea, Prince Edward Island, Toronto, New York, Canada\n- Companies: McClelland and Stewart, Frederick A. Stokes Company\n- Concepts: children's novel, fictional community\n\nFacts:\n- Lucy Maud Montgomery was born on November 30, 1874, and died on April 24, 1942.\n- Lucy Maud Montgomery was a Canadian author who published as L.M. Montgomery.\n- Lucy Maud Montgomery is best known for a series of novels that began in 1908 with Anne of Green Gables.\n- Anne Shirley is the orphaned central character of Anne of Green Gables, and the character made Lucy Maud Montgomery famous in her lifetime and gave her an international following.\n- Avonlea is a fictional community on Prince Edward Island, Canada.\n- Avonlea is the setting of Anne of Green Gables, its sequels, and the television series Road to Avonlea.\n- Anne of Ingleside is a children's novel by Lucy Maud Montgomery.\n- Anne of Ingleside was first published in July 1939 by McClelland and Stewart in Toronto and by the Frederick A. Stokes Company in New York.",
